From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mecid <mecidi.cc@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 12:43:57 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] plat/cix: sky1: TrustZone configuration in BL31

The CIX BL31 reads trustzone_config.bin (firmware header image type 9,
written by the CIX trustzone_config tool) between bl31_platform_setup()
and the runtime services, and the public tree lacks that code.  Add it
as the CIX BL31 behaves (v2.7 release Beta 2.1.5):

* sky1_tz_config.c: read the configuration through spi_nor.c, check the
  TZCF signature, version 1.0 and the tool's double checksum over the
  `length` bytes; use the defaults (SPE on, no secure storage, no
  bootloader3 recovery) when it is missing or invalid.  Both the 40-byte
  files of the current tool and the 36-byte file of the older tool
  Radxa ships for the Orion O6 are accepted.  The 11 data bytes go to
  0x80400000 (mapped secure, as in the CIX BL31) for the secure OS.
* SPE for the Non-secure world follows spe_feature_en: a weak
  plat_spe_for_ns_enabled() hook in manage_extensions_nonsecure(), where
  the CIX BL31 calls spe_enable() or spe_disable().
* A secure storage region that overlaps the flash header or an image it
  lists is dropped with a warning.  The Radxa O6 configuration places it
  at 6 MiB, inside a bootloader3 larger than 1.9 MiB; the secure OS would
  write its NOR file system over UEFI.  The CIX BL31 does not check.
* cix_spi_nor.c: plat_get_nor_data() (bootloader1 flash table) and the
  firmware header lookup move out of the BL2 io storage code so that
  BL31 can use them.
